## Summary
Four people have been arrested in connection with the deaths of 18 elephants in Kenya. Preliminary tests suggest the elephants may have died from cyanide poisoning. The incident highlights ongoing threats to wildlife from poaching and toxic substances.

## Key Points
- Four individuals were arrested following the death of 18 elephants in Kenya
- Preliminary tests indicate possible cyanide poisoning as the cause of death
- The mass elephant deaths represent a significant wildlife loss
- Investigations are ongoing to confirm the cause and those responsible


